<p class="text-xl leading-relaxed text-primary/80 font-medium italic mb-8 border-l-4 border-secondary pl-6">The best facial cosmetic surgery is the one that corrects the underlying cause of what bothers you — not the one with the trendiest name. For structural issues like a receding chin, prominent jaw, or imbalanced nose, skeletal procedures such as orthognathic surgery, genioplasty, and rhinoplasty deliver the most lasting change. For skin and volume concerns, soft-tissue surgery and non-surgical treatments can refine the result.</p>
<div class="bg-surface-container-lowest p-6 rounded-xl border border-surface-container-high my-10 not-prose shadow-sm">
